# =============================================================================
# Proprietary SEGA content -- MUST never be committed (copyright)
# =============================================================================
# BIOS / ROM dump folders
BIOS*/
[Bb]ios*/
roms/
roms_diag*/
MIE/
# SEGA ROM chip dumps (BIOS, cartridge mask ROMs, boot ROMs)
*.ic25
*.ic27
*.ic31
*.ic606
epr-*
mpr-*
opr-*
fpr-*
# JVS / MIE device ROMs and NVRAM/EEPROM dumps
315-*.bin
sp500*.bin
*_eeprom.bin
main_eeprom.bin
x76f100_eeprom.bin
# packed romsets and disc images
*.zip
*.chd
# any raw binary: proprietary dumps and our own build outputs alike.
# The shippable ROMs are distributed via GitHub Releases, not committed.
*.bin

# =============================================================================
# Build artifacts
# =============================================================================
*.o
*.elf
*.map
*.dis
.build_*
# generated per-language copy (see audio_clips_*.h)
src/audio_clips.h

# =============================================================================
# Test / debug outputs
# =============================================================================
# rendered audio samples and MAME captures
*.wav
mame_*.txt
tm_dbg.txt
# MAME screenshots
snap/
# huge `mame -listxml` dump (regenerate for `make cartdb`)
mamelist.xml

# =============================================================================
# Local dev tooling (large / machine-specific, regenerated on demand)
# =============================================================================
# Piper Python venv
tools/.venv/
# Piper voice models (~60 MB each, downloadable)
tools/voices/

# ad-hoc probe/fault Lua scripts (kept local, not part of the shipped set)
mame/id_probe.lua
mame/n2_probe.lua
mame/n2_dev.lua
mame/testmode*.lua
mame/diag_snap*.lua
mame/elan_fault.lua
mame/sram_fault.lua
fault_dbg.lua

